  "articleBody": "A felony drug charge is incredibly serious and can have life-altering consequences, so understanding what you're up against is the first step toward building a strong defense. Unlike misdemeanors, felony convictions often involve lengthy prison sentences, substantial fines, and a permanent mark on your record that can affect your employment, housing, and even voting rights for years to come. The specifics depend on factors like the type and quantity of the drug, your prior criminal history, and whether the offense involved sale, manufacturing, or trafficking. The prosecution will work hard to secure a conviction, so you need someone equally dedicated fighting for you. An experienced felony drug crime defense lawyer, like Angelo Reyes, can scrutinize the evidence, challenge how it was obtained, negotiate with prosecutors, and represent you vigorously in court. Don't underestimate the severity of these charges; getting immediate professional legal assistance is paramount to protecting your future and exploring every possible defense strategy.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
}